# Upstream qbe c081897 miscompiles this; qbe 1.2 does not. jnz compares
# only the 32 least significant bits of an l argument to zero (QBE IL,
# "Jumps"), but when the argument folds to a constant, gvn tests 64 bits.
#
#   1 + 0xffffffff = 2^32 has zero low bits, so $f(0) is 0; qbe returns 1.
#
# run: $f 0
export function w $f(w %u) {
@start
	%x =l add 1, 4294967295
	jnz %x, @yes, @no
@yes
	ret 1
@no
	ret 0
}
